.TITLE "cd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the current working directory. It updates the shell environment to a new path, allowing you to navigate the filesystem.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**chdir**

.DIV "TLDR"
**cd path\to\directory**
Changes the current working directory to the specified path.
> __path\to\directory__ the target folder path

**cd ..**
Moves the current working directory up one level to the parent folder.
> 

**cd \**
Changes the current working directory to the root of the current drive.
> 

**cd /d path\to\directory**
Changes the current drive in addition to changing the directory.
> __/d__ drive change flag | __path\to\directory__ the target path

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Use the __/d__ flag when you need to switch between different drives, such as from __C:__ to __D:__. Running __cd__ without arguments in Windows displays the current directory path instead of returning to home.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:dir** **windows:mkdir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/cd__
